WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know our next guest
from his iconic role

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
as Luke Skywalker
in the "Star Wars" films

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:06.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
and his award-winning
voiceover work as the Joker.

00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:08.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
He stars in the second season
of "Knightfall,"

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:10.477 align:start size:94% position:6%
which airs Monday nights
on History.

00:00:10.477 --> 00:00:11.411 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's take a look.

00:00:11.411 --> 00:00:14.714 size:75% position:38%
-The worth of a man,
knight or Templar,

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:17.917 line:92%
is proven in the theater of war.

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:20.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Luciferians count
battle-hardened warriors

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.322 size:75% position:38% line:92%
amongst their number

00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:25.025 align:start size:94% position:6%
with real weapons
at their disposal.

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:28.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
-God demands
we defend his principles,

00:00:28.328 --> 00:00:31.898 line:92%
training complete or not.

00:00:31.898 --> 00:00:34.267 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Line up for combat!

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:41.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
Any man who dies defending
God's will dies a noble death.

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:43.076 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Never forget that.

00:00:43.076 --> 00:00:46.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Please welcome to the show
Mark Hamill, everyone!

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:48.381 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:58.391 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:00:58.391 --> 00:01:08.001 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:01:08.001 --> 00:01:10.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What a joy it is
to have you here.

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:12.906 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's nice being had.
-All right.

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:14.808 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:14.808 --> 00:01:18.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's great.
And that is --

00:01:18.011 --> 00:01:19.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like
that is a Mark Hamill

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:21.281 size:81% position:41%
I have not seen before
in "Knightfall" here.

00:01:21.281 --> 00:01:24.651
-You know what's so great is,
when you get into all that gear,

00:01:24.651 --> 00:01:27.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you look in the mirror,
Mark Hamill's gone.

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:29.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-So, I don't feel like

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:32.659 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have to take any
responsibility for my actions.

00:01:32.659 --> 00:01:33.893 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:36.729 line:92%
'Cause he's highly unlikable.

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:39.833 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's sort of a latter-day
drill sergeant.

00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:40.700 size:78% position:39% line:92%
And he's just brutal.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:45.105
You know, and I have sort of a
rudimentary grasp of religion,

00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:49.676
but he's saying to the troops,
"Once you complete this course,

00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:53.980
you shall become a member
of God's executioners."

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:57.383
I thought, "Wait a minute.
That's my favorite Commandment."

00:01:57.383 --> 00:01:58.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, right.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.418 --> 00:02:00.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Thou shalt not kill."
It's right up there with --

00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:01.321 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah. Way up top.

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:05.358
-Right up there with "Never
covet thy neighbor's wife."

00:02:05.358 --> 00:02:07.127 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.127 --> 00:02:10.063 line:92%
So he's a perplexing guy.

00:02:10.063 --> 00:02:14.801
But like I say, it was unlike
anything I've done before.

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:15.702 line:92%
And that's what you look for.

00:02:15.702 --> 00:02:17.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
At least what I look for
is the challenge.

00:02:17.871 --> 00:02:19.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure.
-Just not repeat yourself.

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:22.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause eventually "Star Wars"
is gonna go away.

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:22.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.976 --> 00:02:25.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you never know.
You never know, yeah.

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:27.080 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And look,
it comes out in December,

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:29.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I only have eight months
of trolling left.

00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:30.750 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I love to tease
the fans online.

00:02:32.719 --> 00:02:34.053 size:78% position:39% line:92%
It drives them crazy.

00:02:34.053 --> 00:02:35.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm sure Disney's
not that happy about it.

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:37.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
But what are they gonna do,
fire me?

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:39.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, right.

00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:43.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like the safest --
the safest job.

00:02:43.296 --> 00:02:45.932 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's too late.
-It's too late.

00:02:45.932 --> 00:02:48.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's too late.
Hey, Fred Armisen!

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:50.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm a big fan.
Oh, my gosh.

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:52.005 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you. Likewise.
-Oh, wow.

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:53.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's a really big night
for Fred.

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:56.075 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Portlandia."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.075 --> 00:02:58.978 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:58.978 --> 00:03:00.446 line:92%
Is there anything he can't do?

00:03:00.446 --> 00:03:01.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There really is nothing
Fred can't do.

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:05.185
-It's shocking -- author, actor,
comedian, drummer.

00:03:05.185 --> 00:03:06.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, he's everything.
-Exactly.

00:03:06.953 --> 00:03:10.723
-One thing that I think
now people know about you

00:03:10.723 --> 00:03:14.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
is you are a preeminent
voiceover actor.

00:03:14.727 --> 00:03:16.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah.
-And so, when you go

00:03:16.596 --> 00:03:18.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
in front of camera
on something like "Knightfall"

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:19.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
or going back
to the "Star Wars" movies,

00:03:19.432 --> 00:03:23.336 align:start size:94% position:6%
is it a lot of adjustment
to get in that kind of acting

00:03:23.336 --> 00:03:25.505
versus your voice acting?
-Well, that's the problem.

00:03:25.505 --> 00:03:30.677
When I read the script, I sort
of had my voiceover head on.

00:03:30.677 --> 00:03:32.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
I didn't really
think it through.

00:03:32.245 --> 00:03:33.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:36.282 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I didn't realize
the undertaking

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:38.318 line:92%
until I went to wardrobe.

00:03:38.318 --> 00:03:41.588 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they just start
putting on layers and boots

00:03:41.588 --> 00:03:44.457 align:start size:94% position:6%
and belts and capes
and shoulder pads.

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:45.959 line:92%
And then just that makeup alone

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:47.927 align:start size:94% position:6%
is over an hour
in the makeup chair.

00:03:47.927 --> 00:03:50.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because there's --
-There's some scars and stuff.

00:03:50.597 --> 00:03:53.366 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Full wig, full mustache,
full beard...

00:03:53.366 --> 00:03:55.635
-Yeah.
-...three or four facial scars.

00:03:55.635 --> 00:03:58.605 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they do aging
on your hands and your face.

00:03:58.605 --> 00:04:00.406 line:92%
It's one of those things, too.

00:04:00.406 --> 00:04:03.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I couldn't shave
my real beard,

00:04:03.142 --> 00:04:05.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause I was doing
something else.

00:04:05.945 --> 00:04:09.949 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:09.949 --> 00:04:11.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, no.
Oh, no.

00:04:11.384 --> 00:04:14.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
The cat's out of the bag.
-See? See?

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:17.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're just
desperate for spoilers.

00:04:17.056 --> 00:04:17.924 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.924 --> 00:04:21.194
They're hoping I just have
a slip and accidentally...

00:04:21.194 --> 00:04:22.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah.
-...you know, reveal all.

00:04:22.262 --> 00:04:24.464 size:81% position:41%
-That one didn't seem
that accidental, yeah.

00:04:24.464 --> 00:04:26.332 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-No, no.

